course: dictionary
lesson: 3862
title: Fracture: a break or crack
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fracture is a break or crack, especially in a bone. Words around a hard word often give clues, and sometimes the author gives the meaning straight away. «Another time a bigger boy pushed Maddie off a wall, and she fractured (cracked) her wrist.» The bracket tells you that fractured means cracked.
explain: Fracture can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a fracture is the break itself. As a verb, to fracture means to break or crack something hard. «The team fractured after the argument» uses the verb in a different way: here it means the team split apart. The words around it show you which meaning fits.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If you read «The team broke apart after the argument», the sentence still makes sense, so split apart is a good meaning. If the swap does not make sense, try another meaning.
fact: A fracture is a break or crack, especially in a bone.
fact: «Fractured» is the past tense of the verb to fracture, so «she fractured her wrist» means she cracked or broke it.
fact: A «hairline fracture» is a very thin crack.
fact: A «greenstick fracture» happens when a child's bone bends on one side and cracks on the other, like a green twig.
fact: If someone may have a fracture, keep them still and get help. Rocks can also fracture, which you may learn about in geography.
exercise: «She fractured (cracked) her wrist.» What does fractured mean here? | Held tightly | *Cracked or broke | Painted bright | Washed carefully
exercise: Ravi says a «hairline fracture» is a huge hole in the bone. What is a hairline fracture? | A huge hole | Hair that has fallen out | A soft pillow | *A very thin crack
exercise: «The team fractured after the argument.» What does fractured mean here? | Got bigger | Won the game | *Split apart | Grew stronger
test: «A child's bone often breaks like a green twig, bending on one side and cracking on the other; this is called a greenstick fracture.» What is a greenstick fracture? | A dry break in a tree branch | A fracture on a green leaf | *A break where the bone bends and cracks, like a green twig | A cut made by a sharp knife
test: To fracture something hard means to break or crack it. Which word is closest in meaning? | Hug | Sleep | Sing | *Crack
exam: In first aid, what should you do if someone may have a fracture? | Pull the bone straight at once | Ignore it until tomorrow | Make them run around to test it | *Keep them still and get help
